{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"The context deltas identify action `7` precisely: it undoes the immediately preceding action (after a right key it matches left; after a destination click it restores the selected-source state). That opens a more meaningful test than treating it as a wait: whether selection survives carrier motion and can retarget a piece across a wrapped boundary. I’ll reproduce that affordance on clones before ruling it out."}}
