{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_91","type":"agent_message","text":"Pristine-entry behavior resolves `7`: it is a neutral turn. Once a carrier has momentum, `4,7,4` advances exactly like three rights; at rest it does nothing. Crucially, it lets autonomous carriers advance without issuing a new direction command, so prior searches over only `1..4` were incomplete. I’m adding `7` to the shortest-alignment probe and rechecking the long key groups."}}
